# LIVE62_V14_* remains the transaction-ABI field name for backward-compatible
# launcher plumbing. Its value is the currently promoted live62 lane, which
# chains the v15 request-safe lane and retains an authenticated same-process
# all-69 resident snapshot head after the first immutable restore. The promoted
# The compatible base additionally retains both an authenticated growing-prefix continuation
# and the exact rendered prompt before decode, so a tool/template re-render that
# differs from raw generated tokens refills only the new turn rather than falling
# back tens of thousands of tokens. Matching raw turns still reuse the immediately
# preceding live head instead of replaying every token since the immutable
# snapshot. It also seals exit checkpoints at
# their new canonical boundary, authenticates the exact v42-to-v44 snapshot
# source transition, and prevents a repeated in-memory prefix hit from skipping
# the all-69 handoff on a new capture branch. V47 requires the complete
# internally authenticated owner tuple before resident reuse, so a stale
# generation or boundary falls through to the all-69 external restore. Its
# outer bootstrap keeps strict tool calling enabled without changing argv or
# the snapshot payload ABI.
readonly LIVE62_V14_ROOT_RELATIVE='artifacts/qualifications/20260903T-live62-snapshot-compatible-v47-create-only'
readonly LIVE62_V14_COMMAND_SHA256='d10bb7d38257ad0608be1b4bbb9154a9e42663975056696c42a685c519ad61fa'
readonly LIVE62_V14_COMMAND_BYTES='22628'
